Dear Andrew,

In order to obtain the latest version of Zelig using install.packages(), you
need to have the latest version of R installed.  This is currently R
2.6.1(but R
2.6.2 will be available on February 8th, and you should install that as soon
as it is available).

After installing R, launch R and type:
  install.packages("Zelig", repos = "http://gking.harvard.edu")

To verify that you have the correct version of Zelig installed, type:
  library(Zelig)
or if you already have Zelig loaded, type:
  packageDescription("Zelig")
and look for the version number.

If you have R 2.5.1 and do not wish to upgrade, you need to download either
the *.tar.gz or *.zip file from CRAN and install manually (refer to the
Zelig manual).

Yours,
Olivia Lau


