this is a general issue.  if you fix vars to the mean (or some other 
number), you're depending on the veracity of the model.  if there isn't 
any X value at the mean (suppose X is dichotomous for example), then you 
are relying on the model to extrapolate to that middle point.

if you use fn=NULL, it conditions on the observed values; with that you 
can then compute the mean sims if you like for example.  you're still 
relying on the model in this second case, but but you're computing the 
average of a bunch of numbers, each of which the model is better able to 
estimate.

Gary

On Tue, 5 Feb 2008,  wrote:

