NULL" instead of fixing everything at their mean, median, or mode, besides
the flexibility of setting more tricky counterfactual conditions that cannot
be easily done in a "setx" command? What is the statistical reason to prefer
or not to prefer "fn = FULL" in a simulation model?

Thanks.

Shige

